    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nThanks for these plugins. I'm trying to set up a custom textobject for `mini.ai`. The idea is to match segments of camel case and pascal case words.\r\n\r\nI have two patterns that work:\r\n\r\n```\r\n[%s%p]()%u?[%l%d]+()\r\n%l()%u+[%l%d]+()\r\n```\r\n\r\nI tried specifying a composed pattern like so:\r\n\r\n```\r\n      {\r\n        '[%s%p]()%u?',\r\n        '%l()%u+',\r\n      },\r\n      '[%l%d]+()',\r\n```\r\n\r\nbut this doesn't work because the last pattern doesn't have two captures in it:\r\n\r\n```\r\nCould not extract proper positions (two or four empty captures) from string 'o' with extraction pattern '[%l%d]+()'.\r\n```\r\n\r\nI would have thought that due to how composed patterns work (creating the cartesian product of its components) then the final patterns would have two captures?\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.0\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nConfigure the following:\r\n\r\n```\r\nrequire('mini.ai').setup({\r\n    S = {\r\n      {\r\n        '[%s%p]()%u?',\r\n        '%l()%u+',\r\n      },\r\n      '[%l%d]+()',\r\n    },\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nComposed pattern would generate valid textobject patterns\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nComposed pattern is rejected due to not having enough captures:\r\n\r\n```\r\nCould not extract proper positions (two or four empty captures) from string 'o' with extraction pattern '[%l%d]+()'.\r\n```",
