        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thanks for your fast response! Unfortunately it doesn't work. But the patterns work individually for my target cases:\r\n\r\nwhere `[...]` indicates what is selected:\r\n\r\n```\r\n[%s%p]()%u?[%l%d]+()\r\n\r\n[foo]Bar\r\n[Foo]Bar\r\n    [Foo]Bar\r\nbaz.[foo]Bar\r\nbaz.[Foo]Bar\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\n%l()%u+[%l%d]+()\r\n\r\nfoo[Bar]\r\n    Foo[Bar]\r\nbaz.foo[Bar]\r\nbaz.Foo[Bar]\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen I combine them like you suggested, the matches of the second part (the `Bar`s) still works, but the matches of the first part become inconsistent.\r\n\r\nThese cases still work:\r\n\r\n```\r\n    [Foo]Bar\r\nbaz.[foo]Bar\r\nbaz.[Foo]Bar\r\n```\r\n\r\nbut not these ones:\r\n\r\n```\r\n[foo]Bar\r\n[Foo]Bar\r\n```\r\n\r\nso perhaps it's related to these being at the start of the line?\r\n\r\nIndeed, if I explicitly add a pattern to match newline it works as expected:\r\n\r\n```\r\n    S = { {\r\n      '^()%u?[%l%d]+()',\r\n      '[%s%p]()%u?[%l%d]+()',\r\n      '[%l%u]()%u+[%l%d]+()'\r\n    } },\r\n```\r\n\r\nAfter playing around with it some more, I'm satisfied with this, so feel free to close this issue--though not sure if that newline inconsistency is to be expected or not. In any case, thanks again for an amazing set of plugins!",
